  "Question": "\\(\\theta\\) is between \\(0^\\circ\\) and \\(90^\\circ\\), inclusive, and \\(\\cos\\theta=1\\). Find \\(\\sin\\theta\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "0",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "In this range, \\(\\cos\\theta=1\\) only when \\(\\theta=0^\\circ\\), and the sine is 0.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the square-sum identity\n\nThe square-sum identity lets us find sine without first finding the angle. Since \\(\\cos\\theta=1\\),\n\\[\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\cos^2\\theta=1-1^2=0.\\]\nThe only real number whose square is zero is zero, so \\(\\sin\\theta=0\\).",
